        <item>
         <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="about_detector_layout">
          <property name="spacing">
           <number>6</number>
          </property>
          <item>
           <widget class="QLabel" name="label">
            <property name="font">
             <font>
              <bold>true</bold>
             </font>
            </property>
            <property name="text">
             <string>About the YASA REM detector</string>
            </property>
           </widget>
          </item>
          <item>
           <widget class="QLabel" name="textEdit">
            <property name="text">
             <string>The detector of YASA [1] builds on the methods proposed by Yetton et al. [2] and Agarwal et al. [3], mainly on the approach of Agarwal et al.: an amplitude threshold applied to the negative product of the filtered LOC and ROC signals. With this technique, it finds the peaks of the signal and computes, for each REM, its duration, the absolute values of LOC and ROC at its peak, and the absolute rise and fall slopes of both signals.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;With "Remove outliers" ("Detector Step"), the outliers are detected with an Isolation Forest (scikit-learn) and removed from the detected REMs. This step is applied only when at least 50 REMs are detected.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;All the characteristics are computed on the LOC and ROC signals filtered in the REM frequency band of "Detector Step".</string>
            </property>
            <property name="textFormat">
             <enum>Qt::TextFormat::RichText</enum>
            </property>
            <property name="wordWrap">
             <bool>true</bool>
            </property>
            <property name="variant" stdset="0">
             <string notr="true">help</string>
            </property>
           </widget>
          </item>
